      "source": [
        "# DermAI V2: Zero-Cost Massive Training (Kaggle Notebook)\n",
        "\n",
        "**The Secret to Free Compute:** Instead of struggling with Google Colab's 70GB disk limit and running out of space, we are going to train directly inside **Kaggle Notebooks**. \n",
        "\n",
        "Kaggle gives you **30 hours a week of free Dual T4 GPUs**, and more importantly, competition datasets (like the 30GB+ ISIC dataset) mount instantly as read-only drives at `/kaggle/input/`. There are **zero downloads** and **zero disk space issues**.\n",
        "\n",
        "### How to Run This:\n",
        "1. Log into your Kaggle account and go to the [ISIC 2024 Challenge](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/isic-2024-challenge/data) (make sure you accepted the rules).\n",
        "2. Click **\"New Notebook\"** in the top right.\n",
        "3. Go to `File` -> `Import Notebook` and upload this `.ipynb` file.\n",
        "4. **CRITICAL STEP:** In the right sidebar under **Data**, ensure the `isic-2024-challenge` dataset is listed. If it is not, click **\"Add Data\"**, search for `isic-2024-challenge`, and add it to the notebook.\n",
        "5. In the right sidebar, click **Session Options** -> **Accelerator** -> select **GPU T4 x2**."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": None,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
